{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_transient_localises_blowup","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_transient_localises_blowup","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_transient_localises_blowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_transient_localises_blowup","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_transient_localises_blowup.lean#L99-L122","doc":"**Transient trace localises to the blow-up centres**\n    ([`lem:topological-mass-cat-transient`]).\n\nGiven the support hypothesis `hsupp` (the transient component\n`α − τ̂ₙ(α)` lies in the span of the local kernels `ker 𝔡ᵢ`, `i < N`),\nthere are local pieces `cᵢ ∈ ker 𝔡ᵢ` such that\n`tr(α − τ̂ₙ(α)) = Σ_{i<N} tr(cᵢ)`, i.e. the trace is a sum of local\ncontributions `tr_trans(ϱ, pᵢ) := tr(cᵢ)`.  *Derived*: split by the\nsupport hypothesis, then distribute the linear trace (`map_sum`).  When\nthe kernels are disjoint (`hindep`), the pieces are unique\n(`CatTransient.localPiece_unique`), so the local contributions are well\ndefined. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:topological-mass-cat-transient","label":"lem:topological-mass-cat-transient","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-cat-transient.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.localPiece_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.localPiece_unique","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_transient_localises_blowup.lean#L68-L94","doc":"**Uniqueness of the local split under disjointness.**  If the local\nkernels are independent, two splits of the same element over the first\n`N` centres agree piece by piece. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.exists_localPieces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.exists_localPieces","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_transient_localises_blowup.lean#L58-L66","doc":"**Existence of the local split.**  If the transient component lies in\nthe span of the local kernels at the first `N` centres, it is a sum of\npieces `cᵢ ∈ ker 𝔡ᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.localKer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.CatTransient.localKer","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TopologicalMass/cat_transient_localises_blowup.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The local kernel `ker 𝔡_{n+1}|_{pᵢ}` at the `i`-th blow-up centre. ","signatureChunk":0}]}